**House Gaathenaar**  (/'*gaːθenaːr*/, *[[arethian|Arethian]]*: Γαθεναρ) are one of the four [[enkoan-trading-houses|Enkoan Trading Houses]].  They are the head of the Gaathenaar Trade League and are known for their large finance and accurate investments. 

## Etymology
A amalgamation of *Gaat*, meaning wealth, and *Henaar*, meaning keeper.

## Coat of Arms
The Grape bunch on their Coat of Arms signifies the lucrative profits they gained from trading Wine across the world.

## History
House Gaathenaar is said to be founded by Beren Gaathenaar. He was one of the sons of Wylan Seagrin and inherited his keen eye for finances and investment. Therefrom the Gaathenaar Trade League is quite selective about the trade they execute and the investments they make, but they always seem to find the right investment and have grown wealthy of these choices.

Throughout the years they have, as a result of their success, built up influence in the markets of many nations. They use this influence on governments who would oppose them.
